{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
  "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So, here, the district court, I understand, didn't think it was challenging the validity of the order, or that you were, of -- of the FDC interpretation. It was interpreting it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You create the problem that you have here, where the court of appeals says to the -- to the world: We don't have to harmonize the rule, the FCC's rule, with the statute. We can impose liability on someone under a rule that's set, and slavishly have to follow the rules set by the FCC."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what -- what separation of powers problem do you create?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are those unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and I would -- and I would construe the silence here in favor of saying we ought to have judicial review, but it -- but, in some ways, it goes back to Justice Gorsuch's question, and it -- it's part of my problem with the -- with the EPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that your point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hara",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When a district court refuses to accept a final order of the FCC interpreting the TCPA on the basis that it's inconsistent with the statute, that court is determining the validity of the order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the very basic argument, someone who is going to be subject to an enforcement proceeding has a right to notice and an opportunity to be heard on the issue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, can I --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hara",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HARA: It's the underlying merits of the interpretation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Is there any different standard used at the D.C. Circuit when it comes up like that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Prior, adequate, and exclusive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But, counsel, though, you know, you -- you -- you point us to the word \"exclusive,\" but there are more words after that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kovner (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so, here, a party came before the court and said here is the rule that the agency has made about what unsolicited advertisement means. If the Court declines to follow it, it has to do it for a reason."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So you disagree with Respondents on that point? Because Respondents seem to suggest that once it got to the court of appeals, that court had the power to decide whether --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1705",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e9566a75d3278d053d3a243b17ac41590ca002f3f17505e9b8f2fcda60cb9a28",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e9566a75d327-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
